{
  "id": "ep252",
  "duration": 54.42,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 18.94,
      "text": "A dying spacecraft survived its trip to Mercury by sailing on sunlight.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Mariner 10.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mariner_10.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 9.467,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 9.467,
          "end": 18.933,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 18.94,
      "end": 25.82,
      "text": "In November 1973, NASA launched Mariner 10 to attempt the very first interplanetary gravity assist.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Atlas-Centaur launch with Mariner 10.jpg",
        "credit": "Unknown author",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Atlas-Centaur_launch_with_Mariner_10.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 18.933,
          "end": 25.833,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 25.82,
      "end": 31.1,
      "text": "Soon after takeoff, camera heaters failed and peeling paint tricked the star-tracker into losing its guide star.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "02799-National-Air-and-Space-Museum (27207401842).jpg",
        "credit": "xiquinhosilva",
        "license": "CC BY 2.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:02799-National-Air-and-Space-Museum_(27207401842).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 25.833,
          "end": 28.167,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 28.167,
          "end": 31.1,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 31.1,
      "end": 37.14,
      "text": "When attitude control gas ran critically low, engineers gambled on a completely untested maneuver.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "1873 A. and C. Black Map or Chart of the Solar System - Geographicus - SolarSystem-black-1873.jpg",
        "credit": "http://www.geographicus.com/mm5/cartographers/black.txt",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1873_A._and_C._Black_Map_or_Chart_of_the_Solar_System_-_Geographicus_-_SolarSystem-black-1873.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 31.1,
          "end": 34.133,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 34.133,
          "end": 37.133,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 37.14,
      "end": 43.28,
      "text": "Controllers angled the solar panels to catch the pressure of solar radiation, using sunlight itself as a rudder.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 37.133,
          "end": 43.267,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 43.28,
      "end": 49.38,
      "text": "That brilliant improvised fix let Venus fling the probe toward Mercury for three historic flybys.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "PIA03101 Mercury's Southern Hemisphere.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL.",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PIA03101_Mercury%27s_Southern_Hemisphere.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 43.267,
          "end": 46.333,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 46.333,
          "end": 49.367,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 49.38,
      "end": 54.07,
      "text": "Without that sunlight-driven escape, no broken ship could ever sail across the inner solar system.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Mariner 10.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mariner_10.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 49.367,
          "end": 54.433,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
